### 2. MOST IMPORTANT REQUIREMENT

The user uploads one unstructured, mixed or partially structured Excel file.

The Excel may contain hundreds or thousands of customer records scattered across many different areas.

The software must:

1. Read every source row.
2. Identify the correct area for each customer.
3. Find all customer records belonging to the same area, even when they appear far apart in the original worksheet.
4. Combine those records into one area-specific dataset.
5. Analyse the address of every customer in that area.
6. Identify streets, roads, colonies, layouts and sub-localities within the area.
7. Group customers by their identified street/locality.
8. Insert a clearly formatted street/locality heading above each group.
9. Place the corresponding customer records directly below that heading.
10. Generate exactly one Excel workbook for each distinct area.
11. Repeat dynamically for every unique area in the uploaded dataset.
12. Package the generated workbooks into a downloadable ZIP.

**ONE AREA = ONE EXCEL FILE.**

**ALL STREETS BELONGING TO THAT AREA MUST APPEAR AS SEPARATE HEADED SECTIONS INSIDE THE SAME AREA EXCEL FILE.**

Do not generate separate Excel workbooks for individual streets.

This is a critical requirement and overrides any earlier instruction suggesting one workbook per street.

