### 11. IMPORTANT GROUPING DETAILS

Consider these cases.

**Case A – Same street, different customers**

All customers belonging to the same validated street group must be placed under one heading.

**Case B – Different streets within the same area**

Keep them under separate headings within the same Excel workbook.

**Case C – Same street name appears in two different areas**

Keep them separated because their parent area is different.

**Case D – Common abbreviations**

The engine may treat verified equivalent address expressions as the same group.

For example, an approved equivalence between `ROAD` and `RD` can be reused.

**Case E – Different numbered streets**

Do not merge `1ST STREET` with `2ND STREET`.

Do not merge `4TH CROSS` with `5TH CROSS`.

**Case F – Ambiguous locality**

Do not guess.

Place the customer under `STREET / LOCALITY NOT IDENTIFIED` inside the correct area workbook and flag the record for review.

**Case G – Existing source section headings**

Use the heading as contextual evidence but verify the customer address where possible.

**Case H – Locality within locality**

If the same street name exists in two different sub-localities within one area, retain the sub-locality in the group identity.

